========================================================================
Methodological acknowledgements
========================================================================

CamGeo's methodology is inspired by two open reference projects. No code or
data from these projects is included in this repository.

1. MapBiomas (Brazil) — https://mapbiomas.org
   Annual land use and land cover mapping approach: biome-by-biome
   classification in Google Earth Engine, annual numbered collections, and
   open method documents (ATBDs) published with each release.
   MapBiomas data is distributed under CC-BY-SA; MapBiomas code repositories
   carry their own licences (including GPL-3.0 and MPL-2.0 depending on the
   repository). None of their code or data is redistributed here.

2. FLAIR-HUB (IGN, France) — https://ignf.github.io/FLAIR/
   AI-ready dataset design: expert annotation, multi-sensor inputs, open
   benchmarks, and dataset distribution on Hugging Face.
   FLAIR-HUB data and models are distributed under Licence Ouverte 2.0
   (Etalab). None of their code or data is redistributed here.

========================================================================
Input data sources (used as processing inputs; redistributed only where
their licence explicitly allows it)
========================================================================

- Sentinel-1 / Sentinel-2 imagery (Copernicus programme, ESA) — free and open
- Landsat imagery (USGS/NASA) — public domain
- SRTM / Copernicus DEM — free and open
- CHIRPS rainfall (UCSB) — public
- OpenStreetMap — Open Database Licence (ODbL); used only as input features,
  no OSM database is republished (see docs/DATA_POLICY.md)
- WRI / MINFOF Forest Atlas of Cameroon — per-layer licences; verify each
  layer before reuse
- Cam-ForestNet research dataset — mixed licences (parts CC-BY-4.0; Planet
  imagery under NICFI terms — never redistributed)

If you believe this file omits a required attribution, please open an issue.
